  "sex": "not reported",
  "height_cm": null,
  "weight_kg": null
 },
 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Pure moments (paired vacuum-operated low-friction glass cylinders on a loading jig at L1) in flexion, extension, left/right axial torque and right/left lateral bending, applied separately in equal steps to 10 Nm; 3 load-unload cycles with 30 s creep at each step; stereophotogrammetry at each step of the 3rd cycle (angular SE 0.2 deg); sacrum (or both ilia) potted and fixed; no preload.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model the L1-S1 ligamentous spine without iliolumbar ligaments; fix the sacrum, apply pure moments to L1, other vertebrae free; no preload",
   "Apply flexion, extension, left/right axial torque and right/left lateral bending separately in 2.5 Nm steps to 10 Nm (3 load-unload cycles, 30 s creep per step; use the 3rd loading cycle)",
   "Report each level's main rotation (L1-L2 ... L5-S1) in the plane of the moment, measured from the neutral (unloaded) position",
   "Compare the 10 Nm rotation with mean ± SD"
  ],
  "notes": "ROM = NZ + EZ, measured from the neutral position to the 10 Nm point of the 3rd cycle (one direction, not a range). The specimens were also tested with 50/100/150 N preloads (along the L2-L5 body-centre line); these were reported as not statistically different and only the no-preload results are given. Iliolumbar ligaments were removed; with them intact, L5-S1 motion dropped by about 5 deg in FE and 1.5 deg in bilateral LB (Discussion). Mean disc degeneration grade 2.4-2.8 per level (macroscopic, Nachemson). Same laboratory as Panjabi 1994 (100 N preload); specimen overlap not stated (age ranges differ). Neutral zone and elastic zone (Table 1) are not extracted: NZ is defined one-sided from the neutral position and averaged over +/- loads, unlike the both-directions NZ used elsewhere.",
  "subject_model": null
 },
